<title>SWITZERLAND: Ciba, Zeneca settle patent row.</title>
<headline>Ciba, Zeneca settle patent row.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ciba-Geigy AG said it and British firm Zeneca Group Plc had reached agreement to end a patent dispute in all territories over the herbicide propaquizafop.  </p>
<p>&quot;Details of the settlement are confidential but Ciba will continue sales of the products containing propaquizafop,&quot; Ciba said in a statement. Ciba did not elaborate.</p>
<p>The dispute concerned a crop protection product with the brand name Agil, whose active ingredient is the herbicide propaquizafop. It is used as a herbicide in broad-leaved crops such as oilseed rape and sugar beet.</p>
<p>Zeneca had claimed in patent infringement suits filed in several countries that propaquizafop infringed on a patent that Zeneca licenses from ICI Australia.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
